WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.826
Hi! Conjunctions are like bridges that join two ideas. Today we'll learn although, despite and unless, and some conjunctions that come in pairs.

2
00:00:11.976 --> 00:00:17.946
First, a quick review. Because gives a reason: I stayed home because I was sick.

3
00:00:18.096 --> 00:00:22.170
So gives a result: I was sick, so I stayed home.

4
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.914
Although and despite show contrast. They mean that something happens even though something else is true.

5
00:00:29.064 --> 00:00:32.610
Unless means if not.

6
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:39.618
Although is followed by a full clause with a subject and a verb: Although it was raining, we played outside.

7
00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:45.066
Despite is followed by a noun: Despite the rain, we played outside.

8
00:00:45.216 --> 00:00:52.098
Despite can also be followed by a verb with -ing: Despite feeling tired, she finished the race.

9
00:00:52.248 --> 00:00:59.562
Unless: You will be late unless you hurry. That means if you don't hurry, you'll be late.

10
00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:07.122
Some conjunctions come in pairs. Not only... but also: She is not only clever but also kind.

11
00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:16.122
Neither... nor means not one and not the other: Neither Tom nor Amy likes durians. Neither is already negative, so don't add not.

12
00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:24.738
Either... or means one of the two: You can have either tea or juice. Paired conjunctions must stay together.

13
00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:29.826
Watch out! Although he was tired, but he kept running is wrong!

14
00:01:29.976 --> 00:01:36.786
In Chinese we say both words, but in English although already shows the contrast, so we can't add but.

15
00:01:36.936 --> 00:01:44.370
Say: Although he was tired, he kept running. Or: He was tired, but he kept running.

16
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:55.362
Your turn! ___ the heavy traffic, we reached school on time. Although or Despite? Pause and think.

17
00:01:55.512 --> 00:02:04.290
The answer is Despite, because it's followed by a noun, the heavy traffic, not a full clause. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:15.210
Another one! You cannot go out ___ you finish your homework. Which connector fits? Pause and think.

19
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:23.778
The answer is unless. It means if you don't finish your homework, you can't go out. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:23.928 --> 00:02:34.266
Last one! Neither my father ___ my mother can swim. What goes in the blank? Pause and think.

21
00:02:34.416 --> 00:02:40.962
The answer is nor. Neither goes with nor. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:41.112 --> 00:02:52.338
One more! She ran fast. She missed the bus. How do you join them using although? Pause and think.

23
00:02:52.488 --> 00:03:01.266
The answer is: Although she ran fast, she missed the bus. Notice there is no but. Did you get it right?

24
00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:13.986
Remember: although takes a clause, despite takes a noun or an -ing verb. Unless means if not. Paired conjunctions stay together, and although never goes with but in the same sentence.

25
00:03:14.136 --> 00:03:18.306
Try saying a sentence with despite!

